<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pandya dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pandya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pandya dynasty was a long-lived Tamil ruling house of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai">Madurai</a>. In the early fourteenth century the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malik-kafur">Malik Kafur</a>, serving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-khalji">Alauddin Khalji</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>, sacked the Pandya treasury at Madurai. The campaign was part of the submission of most major southern powers to the sultanate by 1311.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty.jpg" alt="Pandya dynasty" width="320" height="299" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Borders by Rawn3012 using GIMP · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Pandya_dynasty_at_its_apex.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
